  "body": "﻿Process change: a P1/P2 filed after a minor/major cut has started does not restart the cut. The P1/P2 rule is checked once at the start of the cut (release step 1), the release PR body records that check, and a late P1/P2 is named under \"Known issues\" and ships in the next minor. Only the maintainer can stop a cut for one.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/1424-late-p1-p2-no-restart.md (quotes the maintainer, 2026-11-13).\n\nFiles: AGENTS.md (Priorities bullet, fix-tests sentence, release steps 1-3), .claude/PROCESS_VERSION 54 -> 55.\n\nChecked: the touched text reads correctly against its neighbours. No build or gate run (docs and process only). The skills under .claude/skills/ do not repeat the P1/P2 rule (merge-ready tests for an open release/* PR, which stays true), so they are unchanged.\n\nProcess changes: PROCESS_VERSION 55. Forks sync the process files at the next session start; no code change.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1424\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
